{"body":{"text":["I don't know. Maybe you're stopping short of it here. I said I want to think this through. I want to do the right and the powerful thing here. So don't stop short. There is something here. There's the opportunity. There's the potency of making the right kind of structure here. So I don't think a session is divided into its sequences or purposes. I think an elevation comes down into a start and an end point. That's one way, right? So you're kind of quarantining the utterances, meaning it's in here. Sometimes there's a very clear end, right? The sessions can be different. The session may be more pure, and that's deliberate for me sometimes. I want to keep focus on one thing at a time. A question arises, we work through that question, then we stop that and we continue with something else. Then we have a very clean cut. But in this session, I've been talking about many things at once. So what does that mean? What's the right way of typing structure here? Yeah, I want to use grounding. I really do. This is something that the rule did before, and it was really powerful in the very limited way it did it. So in the rule, we'd have, for example, a project where we have various interviews with people using the application, and so they're in the whole long. And then from that, we built all the workflows of the application. And then the way that the rule worked was that each brief would end in an italic paragraph. And so there you state the condition of the brief as a ratification measure and settledness measure and so on. But there you'd also write where this brief comes from. So a workflow might then say in there, hey, this information comes from this part of the interview when we talk about that. And then from there, we'd also do other things. We'd chart the application and how the application works and build a schematic of the application reflected in the hierarchy. So we have various sources and they all come grounding together. And then, the next thing is that we're building requirements and then we can link them. So the kind of grounding is really interesting, and the briefs had this kind of ratification or measures paragraph in the end. And so that's kind of where the connection came in. It's a very multi-purpose thing. I'm not saying we are to adopt that. I'm just saying it gives an experience of sources and grounding that is really powerful. So here we're doing the successor of that in the very system that I've been envisioning for a long while. Yeah, the system's not fully built yet, but at least we have the primitives to you and me here decide on a strong starting point for how we build this kind of graph. So of course, as you cite something in the knowledge holon, you might be citing an elevation. That elevation might then be, so that's what I'm still exploring. How does this connect really? Because a session is just words. So how do we categorize? How do we map meaning in here? I think you can be the right sparring partner here if you give yourself the freedom and effort to explore this with me and mirror what we're exploring. I've just stated something. I've made a little bit of progression, but there is an edge where things feel a little bit abstract. So let's see if we in tandem here can expand the boundaries until we find what makes sense here."]},"id":"1M89HT470QJ7000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
